{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/734411-cardians-vegas-a-nwod-hunter-chronicle-meet-greet-oct-30th-7-pm-pst","id":734411,"title":"Cardians: Vegas - A nWoD Hunter chronicle (Meet & Greet Oct. 30th 7 PM PST)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-28T05:24:06-07:00","id":734411,"title":"Cardians: Vegas - A nWoD Hunter chronicle (Meet & Greet Oct. 30th 7 PM PST)","content":"<a href=\"http://cardians.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Cardians</a> is a group on DeviantART dedicated to hosting several nWoD Hunter chronicles based on a custom Conspiracy of the same name. First, a little background:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>A criminal syndicate known for naming their ranks after card suits. Its inner workings are generally unknown; it is presumed that the lack of information available on this organization is not accidental, but intentionally made to be, under the direction of a powerful guiding hand.<br /> <br /> The Cardians as a whole operate as a Family. Per their namesake, each Family member is assigned to a suit - the highest ranked members of each suit are likely given ranks after face cards, while the indisputable leaders of each suit could be referred to as Aces. A leader, presumably of higher rank than of an Ace, is rumored to exist at the top of the hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Unlike most Hunter groups, the Cardians are somewhat more willing to tolerate benevolent monsters -- they themselves are quite at home in the shadows, where they prefer to keep their operations in the first place, and they can often find uses for a voluntary monster\u2019s talents. Regardless, they are not to be confused for a charity; the Cardians are first and foremost a Hunter conspiracy, one that has no qualms abandoning the moral high ground to keep the Vigil. They are above all interested in maintaining the curtain that separates the mundane from the extraordinary; any who dare disrupt or compromise that curtain, abandon or betray the Vigil or the Family, or prove themselves a detriment to the Family\u2019s ends are </i></span></span><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>dealt with,</i></span></span></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> in a swift and discreet manner. Human, Cardian, or otherwise.</i><br /> <br /> <i>On the other hand, it is rumored that some monsters are even allowed to walk freely within their ranks. If they do, it is a testament to the Family\u2019s strength and influence that it hasn\u2019t simply been wiped off the map by other, less sympathetic Hunters. Despite their colorful past with the other Hunter conspiracies, however, the Cardian Syndicate remains large enough, and resourceful enough, to protect and even fully financially support their more </i></span></span><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>inhuman</i></span></span></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> associates.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Cardian compacts maintain a strong presence on the East and West Coasts of the United States, with varying states of occupancy inland. Other bases of operation have been theorized to exist the world over, but a dearth of evidence can neither prove nor disprove these claims.</i><br /> <br /> <i>It is generally considered unwise to cross any member of the Cardian Conspiracy, for where one Cardian lurks, her Family is surely close behind.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> Cardians: Vegas is one of these said compacts, or more commonly known as divisions, that centers itself in America's playground. The city's underbelly is awash with creatures of every sort as a myriad of factions duke it out for dominance and fortune. The turbulent sea changes as much as the opulent face that covers it, and this division in smack dab in the middle of it all, trying to get its own slice of a very small pie.<br /> <br /> The game is played over Skype using Roll20 for rolls and atmosphere. We'll be using GMC rules, with a few little house rules sprinkled here and there. If you're interested, you'll need DeviantART, Skype, and Roll20 accounts if you don't already have them (all free, so no worries). After that, you'll need to <a href=\"http://cardians.deviantart.com/journal/Application-to-Cardians-473382426\" target=\"_blank\">apply for Cardians</a> and then attend the meet &amp; greet happening on <b>October 30th, 7 PM PST</b>. The meet and greet is made to see which potential players get along so that we can select the right members for our division.<br /> <br /> Don't fret if you can't make it to the meet &amp; greet, as there's a good chance we'll host another one (this one is our second, actually) and even if you don't get in the division right away, we'll have openings for more players in the future, not to mention there will be more divisions taking in members as well.<br /> <br /> In any case, good luck, and if you have any questions, don't be afraid to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}